            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> 12\\. You can also (already) redefine mappings dynamically, including `<expr>` mappings, so dot-repeat is already \"dynamic\", so my objection doesn't really hold.\n>          Your previous comment is too long, please summarize it in one sentence. Are you asking for `setrepeat(<function>)` ?\n\nsorry for the too long comment. because my english is poor, so I used ai and it seems comment too long. \nIn summary, I want to append a lua function into redo stream, and I already find that the only lua function can be called in redo is `vim.paste`, so I tried to hack it to call any luafunction. and it works, the lua function can call any vim api with no bug like textlock or other timelock, etc. \n\nSo I think if we make another api to register a luafunction in a redo stream, then we don't need to hack vim.paste to call luafunction in dot_repeat. \n\nIf we make this api, any plugins editing text in insert mode, like completion, autopair, ..., they can append a luafunction into redo stream and support dot repeat natively, not by `<expr>`. ",
